365 L 2138 4365 z\nM 2144 384 Q 2675 384 2988 614 Q 3302 845 3302 1235 Q 3302 1530 3142 1715 Q 2982 1901 2624 1984 L 1792 2189 Q 1696 2214 1555 2153 Q 1414 2093 1273 1961 Q 1133 1830 1033 1648 Q 934 1466 934 1248 Q 934 838 1244 611 Q 1555 384 2144 384 L 2144 384 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-81\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-a9\" transform=\"translate(46.5 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-88\" transform=\"translate(67.40625 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_10\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(210.121125 95.888) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><defs><path id=\"LibreFranklin-Regular-86\" d=\"M 2362 4806 Q 2605 4806 2797 4755 Q 2989 4704 3142 4614 Q 3296 4525 3414 4416 Q 3533 4307 3610 4186 Q 3622 4160 3625 4131 Q 3629 4102 3590 4083 L 3226 3936 Q 3194 3917 3168 3933 Q 3142 3949 3130 3974 Q 2989 4141 2813 4243 Q 2637 4346 2368 4346 Q 1907 4346 1609 4122 Q 1312 3898 1171 3510 Q 1030 3123 1030 2637 Q 1030 2534 1049 2502 Q 1069 2470 1146 2509 Q 1389 2630 1670 2732 Q 1952 2835 2330 2835 Q 2822 2835 3171 2652 Q 3520 2470 3702 2156 Q 3885 1843 3885 1446 Q 3885 998 3664 656 Q 3443 314 3068 128 Q 2694 -58 2234 -58 Q 1670 -58 1264 220 Q 858 499 640 1027 Q 422 1555 422 2304 Q 422 3085 656 3645 Q 890 4205 1325 4505 Q 1760 4806 2362 4806 L 2362 4806 z\nM 2259 2387 Q 2093 2387 1885 2345 Q 1677 2304 1491 2240 Q 1306 2176 1171 2093 Q 1094 2042 1068 1987 Q 1043 1933 1043 1818 Q 1043 1587 1116 1340 Q 1190 1094 1334 876 Q 1478 659 1702 524 Q 1926 390 2234 390 Q 2534 390 2768 524 Q 3002 659 3139 896 Q 3277 1133 3277 1421 Q 3277 1690 3155 1910 Q 3034 2131 2803 2259 Q 2573 2387 2259 2387 L 2259 2387 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-80\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-a9\" transform=\"translate(68.796875 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-86\" transform=\"translate(89.703125 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_11\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(322.417675 82.394667) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-80\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-a9\" transform=\"translate(68.796875 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-88\" transform=\"translate(89.703125 0)\"/></g></g></g></g><defs><clipPath id=\"p0a9c5852b4\"><rect x=\"43.373\" y=\"10.824\" width=\"345.96\" height=\"127.512\"/></clipPath></defs></svg>\n","title":"Exhibit 2 · ARR gained per $1 spent","note":null},"answer":"<p>A saves $0.90M of ARR: <b>$1.8 per $1</b>. B saves $0.60M: $0.6 per $1. C adds $1.2M: $0.8 per $1.</p> <p>Kept ARR is worth as much as new ARR: both recur next year. So <b>A is by far the best use of money</b>, then C, then B.</p>"},{"q":"Can Tessera hit 30% next year?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>With A and C: $38.0M (27% growth). Adding B too: $38.6M (29%). All three fall short of $39.0M.</p> <p><b>So-what:</b> tell the board 30% is a stretch. To close the last gap, look at upgrades: 8% expansion is low for analytics software; a paid add-on for existing customers could help.</p>"}],"reco":"Prioritise retention before doubling the sales team. Small businesses make up 20% of ARR but 53% of the ARR lost, so automated onboarding for them is the best use of money: about $1.8 of ARR kept per $1, against $0.8 for extra sales spend. Fund onboarding ($0.5M) and $1.5M of extra sales spend; that gets growth to about 27%. Customer-success managers for mid-market ($1.0M) lift it to about 29%, still short of 30%; the rest has to come from selling more to existing customers. Risk: automated onboarding may not cut churn as much as planned, so pilot it on new sign-ups first.","great":["Builds next year's ARR from churn, downgrades, upgrades and new sales","Finds where churn is concentrated in dollars, not customers","Compares options on ARR per dollar","Tells the board the target is a stretch, with numbers"],"id":55,"slug":"tessera-analytics"}